      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this description needs to be fixed a little bit.\n\nIn PD 2.0, it\u0027s valid for the UFP to issue a DR_Swap because it prefers to be a DFP. There are chargers (in particular, a Google 60W charger from 2015) that are USB PD 2.0, and will Accept a DR_Swap issued by the Sink/UFP (Chromebook).\n\n\nThe real issue here is that in USB PD 2.0, only the DFP is allowed to issue DiscoverIdentity, and a partner\u0027s REJECT to a DR_Swap is allowed too.\n\nI would edit this description as follows:\n\n\"In USB PD 2.0, Discover Identity can only be initiated by the DFP. When a charger that uses USB PD 2.0 is hotplugged, USB-C port\u0027s attempt to swap from UFP to DFP may be rejected.\"",
